['Here's a basic implementation of the function in Java using Spring Boot framework with RetryTemplate for handling API calls and CompletableFuture for parallel processing. This is a simplified version and does not include all the considerations mentioned above. 

```java
import org.springframework.retry.support.RetryTemplate;
import org.springframework.web.client.RestClientException;
import java.util.ArrayList;
import java.util.List;
import java.util.concurrent.CompletableFuture;
import java.util.stream.Collectors;

public class PokemonReportService {
    private final RetryTemplate retryTemplate;
    private final RestTemplate restTemplate;

    public PokemonReportService(RetryTemplate retryTemplate, RestTemplate restTemplate) {
        this.retryTemplate = retryTemplate;
        this.restTemplate = restTemplate;
    }

    public List<PokemonReport> generateReports(List<String> pokemonNames) {
        return pokemonNames.stream()
                .map(pokemonName -> CompletableFuture.supplyAsync(() -> getPokemonData(pokemonName)))
                .collect(Collectors.toList())
                .stream()
                .map(CompletableFuture::join)
                .collect(Collectors.toList());
    }

    private PokemonReport getPokemonData(String pokemonName) {
        try {
            return retryTemplate.execute(retryContext -> {
                try {
                    String url = "https://pokeapi.co/api/v2/pokemon/" + pokemonName;
                    PokemonData data = restTemplate.getForObject(url, PokemonData.class);
                    return new PokemonReport(data.getName(), data.getTypes(), data.getWeaknesses(), data.getResistances(), data.getImmunities());
                } catch (RestClientException e) {
                    throw new RuntimeException("Failed to fetch data for " + pokemonName, e);
                }
            });
        } catch (RuntimeException e) {
            return new PokemonReport(pokemonName, new ArrayList<>(), new ArrayList<>(), new ArrayList<>(), new ArrayList<>());
        }
    }
}
```

This code assumes that there is a `PokemonData` class with methods to get the name, types, weaknesses, resistances and immunities of a Pokemon. The `RestTemplate` is used to make HTTP requests to fetch data from the PokeAPI. 

Please note that this is a simplified version and does not include all the considerations mentioned above such as error handling, performance optimization, scalability etc. For a production-ready solution, you would need to consider these factors in detail.
']

