import java.io.*;
import java.util.concurrent.ConcurrentHashMap;
import javax.imageio.ImageIO;

public class ThemeUtils {
    private static final ConcurrentHashMap<String, Bitmap> themeCache = new ConcurrentHashMap<>();
    private static String defaultThemeDir;

    public static synchronized void initializeDefaultThemeDirectory(String fallbackPath) {
        if (defaultThemeDir == null) {
            File dir = new File(fallbackPath);
            if (!dir.exists()) {
                boolean created = dir.mkdirs();
                if (!created) {
                    System.err.println("Failed to create default theme directory");
                }
            }
            defaultThemeDir = fallbackPath;
        }
    }

    public static StateProvider loadStateObject(String fileName) {
        try (FileInputStream fis = new FileInputStream(fileName);
             ObjectInputStream ois = new ObjectInputStream(fis)) {
            Object obj = ois.readObject();
            if (obj instanceof StateProvider) {
                return (StateProvider) obj;
            } else {
                System.err.println("Loaded object does not implement StateProvider");
                return null;
            }
        } catch (IOException | ClassNotFoundException e) {
            System.err.println("Failed to load state object: " + e);
            return null;
        }
    }

    public static Bitmap getThemeBitmap(String fileName) {
        if (!themeCache.containsKey(fileName)) {
            try {
                File pngFile = new File(defaultThemeDir, fileName + ".png");
                Bitmap bitmap = ImageIO.read(pngFile);
                themeCache.put(fileName, bitmap);
            } catch (IOException e) {
                System.err.println("Failed to parse PNG file: " + e);
            }
        }

        return themeCache.getOrDefault(fileName, null);
    }

    public static void recycleThemeBitmap(String fileName) {
        Bitmap bitmap = themeCache.remove(fileName);
        if (bitmap != null) {
            bitmap.recycle();
        }
    }
}
```
This code uses a `ConcurrentHashMap` to manage the theme cache, which is thread-safe and optimized for high concurrency. It also uses Java's built-in synchronization mechanisms to ensure that only one thread can initialize the default theme directory at a time. 

The `loadStateObject` method reads an object from a file using `ObjectInputStream` and checks if it implements `StateProvider`. If not, or if there is any I/O error, it logs an error message and returns null.

The `getThemeBitmap` method retrieves a bitmap from the cache. If the bitmap is not in the cache, it attempts to parse a PNG file from the default theme directory and add it to the cache. If there is any I/O error or if the file format is inconsistent, it logs an error message but does not crash the application.

The `recycleThemeBitmap` method removes a bitmap from the cache and recycles it, freeing up resources. It also handles the case where the bitmap was already removed from the cache (e.g., if it has been recycled by another thread). 

Please note that this is just an example and may need to be adapted to your specific use case. For instance, you might want to add more sophisticated error handling or logging, or you might want to use a different data structure for the theme cache. Also, please replace `Bitmap` with the actual class of bitmaps in your application.
