['Here is a JavaScript function that meets all the requirements mentioned in the problem statement:

```javascript
function generateFooter(scripts) {
    const footer = document.createElement('div');
    scripts.forEach((scriptObj) => {
        if (!scriptObj.key || !['external', 'internal'].includes(scriptObj.type)) {
            console.warn("Invalid script object: ", scriptObj);
            return;
        }

        let existingScript = document.querySelector(`script[data-key="${scriptObj.key}"]`);
        if (existingScript) {
            footer.removeChild(existingScript);
        }

        const scriptTag = document.createElement('script');
        scriptTag.setAttribute("data-key", scriptObj.key);

        if (scriptObj.type === 'external') {
            scriptTag.src = scriptObj.src;
            scriptTag.async = true;
        } else if (scriptObj.type === 'internal') {
            scriptTag.textContent = scriptObj.innerHTML;
        }

        footer.appendChild(scriptTag);
    });

    return footer.outerHTML;
}
```
This function creates a new `div` element for the footer section, iterates over each script object in the input array, and generates the appropriate HTML based on the type of script. It also handles potential conflicts by removing any existing scripts with the same key before adding a new one. The function returns the outerHTML of the footer div as a string.
