['Here is a basic implementation of your requirements in Rust. This code does not include all the details you requested as it would require a lot more context about what exactly should be compiled, how logging should work, etc. But this should give you an idea of how to structure such a function. 

```rust
use std::process::{Command, Stdio};
use std::time::Instant;
use sync_lazy::SyncLazy;
use log::info;

fn compile_and_measure() -> (i32, u64, u64) {
    let start = Instant::now();
    let before_size = get_resident_set_size().unwrap_or(0);

    let output = Command::new("rustc")
        .arg("--crate-type=lib")
        .arg("your_file.rs")
        .stdout(Stdio::piped())
        .stderr(Stdio::piped())
        .spawn()
        .unwrap();

    let stdout = output.wait_with_output().unwrap();
    let end = Instant::now();
    let after_size = get_resident_set_size().unwrap_or(0);

    if !stdout.status.success() {
        info_hook("Compilation failed: {}", stdout.stderr);
        return (1, before_size, after_size);
    }

    let duration = end.duration_since(start).as_secs();
    info_hook("Compilation succeeded in {} seconds.", duration);
    (0, before_size, after_size)
}

fn get_resident_set_size() -> Result<u64, Box<dyn std::error::Error>> {
    let output = Command::new("ps")
        .arg("-o")
        .arg("rss=")
        .arg(std::process::id().to_string())
        .output()?;

    if !output.status.success() {
        return Err(formatError(output.stderr));
    }

    let rss = String::from_utf8(output.stdout)?.trim().parse()?;
    Ok(rss)
}

lazy_static::lazy_static![
    static ref INFO_HOOK: SyncLazy<dyn Fn(&str, &[u8])> = SyncLazy::new(|| {
        Box::new(|msg, _stderr| info_hook(msg)) as Box<dyn Fn(&str, &[u8])>
    })
];

fn info_hook(msg: &str, stderr: &[u8]){
    let error = String::from_utf8_lossy(stderr);
    info_hook.log(formatError(error));
}
```
This code measures the compilation time and resident set size of a Rust compiler process using `std::process`, `std::time`, and `get_resident_set_size` function respectively. It also uses `SyncLazy` to install an ice hook for logging errors. The `info_hook` function logs the error message if compilation fails.
']

