["Here is a basic implementation of such function using PHP. This code does not cover all your requirements but it gives you an idea about how to start implementing them. 

```php
<?php
class UserService {
    private $authService;
    private $logger;
    private $rateLimiter;
    private $passwordValidator;

    public function __construct(AuthServiceInterface $authService, LoggerInterface $logger, RateLimiterInterface $rateLimiter, PasswordValidatorInterface $passwordValidator) {
        $this->authService = $authService;
        $this->logger = $logger;
        $this->rateLimiter = $rateLimiter;
        $this->passwordValidator = $passwordValidator;
    }

    public function updatePassword($userId, $newPassword) {
        // Validate password strength
        if (!$this->passwordValidator->isStrongEnough($newPassword)) {
            throw new Exception('Password is not strong enough');
        }

        // Check rate limit
        if ($this->rateLimiter->isExceeded($userId)) {
            throw new Exception('Rate limit exceeded');
        }

        $attempts = 0;
        do {
            $attempts++;

            try {
                // Update password in auth service
                $this->authService->updatePassword($userId, $newPassword);

                // Log success
                $this->logger->info('Successfully updated password', ['user_id' => $userId]);

                return;
            } catch (NetworkException $e) {
                // Log network failure
                $this->logger->error('Network error while updating password', ['exception' => $e, 'attempts' => $attempts]);

                // Sleep before retrying
                sleep($attempts);
            } catch (AuthServiceException $e) {
                // Log auth service failure
                $this->logger->error('Error from auth service while updating password', ['exception' => $e, 'user_id' => $userId]);

                throw $e;
            }
        } while ($attempts < 3);

        // Log failed after max attempts
        $this->logger->error('Failed to update password after maximum attempts', ['user_id' => $userId]);
    }
}
?>
```
This code assumes that you have interfaces for AuthServiceInterface, LoggerInterface, RateLimiterInterface and PasswordValidatorInterface. You would need to implement these interfaces according to your specific requirements. 

Please note that this is a simplified example and does not cover all the points in your list. It's recommended to use existing libraries or frameworks for handling such tasks as rate limiting, logging, network errors, etc. Also, you should consider using a message queue system like RabbitMQ or Kafka to handle high concurrency environments.
