['Here is a basic implementation of `HashService` in Java using MD5, SHA-1, and SHA-256 algorithms. This code does not include integration with external data sources or additional hashing standards as per the requirement. 

```java
import java.security.*;
import java.util.*;
import java.nio.charset.StandardCharsets;
import java.time.Duration;
import java.time.Instant;
import java.util.concurrent.ConcurrentHashMap;

public class HashService {
    private static final Map<String, MessageDigest> algorithms = new ConcurrentHashMap<>();
    private static final Map<String, String> cache = new ConcurrentHashMap<>();

    static {
        try {
            algorithms.put("MD5", MessageDigest.getInstance("MD5"));
            algorithms.put("SHA-1", MessageDigest.getInstance("SHA-1"));
            algorithms.put("SHA-256", MessageDigest.getInstance("SHA-256"));
        } catch (NoSuchAlgorithmException e) {
            throw new RuntimeException(e);
        }
    }

    public static String hash(String algorithm, String input) {
        if (input == null || input.length() > 100_000) { // handle large inputs or nulls efficiently
            return null;
        }

        MessageDigest md = algorithms.getOrDefault(algorithm, algorithms.get("MD5")); // default to MD5 if not found
        String cacheKey = algorithm + input;
        String cachedResult = cache.get(cacheKey);

        if (cachedResult != null) {
            logOperation(algorithm, "CACHE", input.length());
            return cachedResult;
        }

        Instant startTime = Instant.now();
        byte[] hashBytes = md.digest(input.getBytes(StandardCharsets.UTF_8));
        StringBuilder sb = new StringBuilder();
        for (byte b : hashBytes) {
            sb.append(String.format("%02x", b));
        }

        Duration duration = Duration.between(startTime, Instant.now());
        logOperation(algorithm, "COMPUTE", input.length(), duration);

        cachedResult = sb.toString();
        cache.put(cacheKey, cachedResult); // update cache
        return cachedResult;
    }

    private static void logOperation(String algorithm, String operationType, int length) {
        System.out.printf("[%s] %s: Length=%d\n", algorithm, operationType, length);
    }

    private static void logOperation(String algorithm, String operationType, int length, Duration duration) {
        System.out.printf("[%s] %s: Length=%d Time=%dms\n", algorithm, operationType, length, duration.toMillis());
    }
}
```
This code uses a `ConcurrentHashMap` for caching and thread safety. It logs the operations with their execution times if they were computed (not from cache). The default hash algorithm is MD5 due to its simplicity and common use cases. 

Please note that this is a basic implementation and does not include error handling or logging of exceptions, which should be added in a production environment. Also, it uses the console for logging operations, but in a real-world scenario, you would likely want to integrate with a centralized logging service like Log4j or SLF4J.
']

