['Here's a basic implementation of the problem using Java's ExecutorService for concurrency, AtomicInteger for thread safety, and UnionFind data structure to find disjoint pairs. Note that this is a simplified version and doesn't include all the features mentioned above like memory management, external service integration, reporting, etc.

```java
import java.util.*;
import java.util.concurrent.*;
import java.util.concurrent.atomic.*;

class UnionFind {
    private int[] parent;
    private byte[] rank;
    private int count;

    public UnionFind(int n) {
        if (n < 0) throw new IllegalArgumentException();
        count = n;
        parent = new int[n];
        rank = new byte[n];
        for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {
            parent[i] = i;
            rank[i] = 0;
        }
    }

    public int find(int p) {
        while (p != parent[p]) {
            parent[p] = parent[parent[p]];  // path compression by halving
            p = parent[p];
        }
        return p;
    }

    public void union(int p, int q) {
        int rootP = find(p);
        int rootQ = find(q);
        if (rootP == rootQ) return;

        // make root of smaller rank point to root of larger rank
        if      (rank[rootP] < rank[rootQ]) parent[rootP] = rootQ;
        else if (rank[rootP] > rank[rootQ]) parent[rootQ] = rootP;
        else {
            parent[rootQ] = rootP;
            rank[rootP]++;
        }
        count--;
    }
}

public class Main {
    private static final int MAX_SEGMENT_SIZE = 10000; // adjust as needed

    public static void main(String[] args) throws InterruptedException, ExecutionException {
        int[] array = new Random().ints(1000000).toArray(); // replace with your actual data

        ExecutorService executor = Executors.newFixedThreadPool(Runtime.getRuntime().availableProcessors());
        List<Future<Integer>> futures = new ArrayList<>();

        AtomicInteger disjointPairsCount = new AtomicInteger(0);

        for (int i = 0; i < array.length; i += MAX_SEGMENT_SIZE) {
            int end = Math.min(array.length, i + MAX_SEGMENT_SIZE);

            futures.add(executor.submit(() -> {
                UnionFind uf = new UnionFind(end - i);

                for (int j = i; j < end; j++) {
                    int root = uf.find(array[j]);

                    if (root != array[j]) {
                        disjointPairsCount.incrementAndGet();
                    } else {
                        uf.union(root, array[j]);
                    }
                }

                return end - i; // return the size of this segment
            }));
        }

        for (Future<Integer> future : futures) {
            System.out.println("Segment size: " + future.get());
        }

        executor.shutdown();

        System.out.println("Total disjoint pairs: " + disjointPairsCount);
    }
}
```
This code creates a thread pool and submits tasks to it for each segment of the array, which are processed concurrently. The `UnionFind` data structure is used to find disjoint pairs in each segment. The total count of disjoint pairs is maintained using an `AtomicInteger` to ensure thread safety.
']

