    while(temp != NULL && temp->data.RNTI != RNTI) {
        temp = temp->next;
    }

    if(temp == NULL) {
        pthread_mutex_unlock(&lock);
        return;
    }

    if(temp->prev != NULL) {
        temp->prev->next = temp->next;
    } else {
        head = temp->next;
    }

    if(temp->next != NULL) {
        temp->next->prev = temp->prev;
    }

    free(temp);

    pthread_mutex_unlock(&lock);
}
```
This code uses a simple doubly linked list with mutexes for thread safety. The `insert` function allocates memory for a new node and adds it to the front of the list. If allocation fails, the function returns without modifying the list. Similarly, the `delete` function searches for a node with a given RNTI and removes it from the list if found.

