The code also includes a basic mechanism for cleaning up unused configurations, but it's very simplistic and doesn't take into account the specific requirements of your system. A real-world implementation would need to consider factors such as how often each configuration is used, how long it has been since it was last accessed or updated, and whether there are any external dependencies that might prevent it from being cleaned up immediately.
