The choice of data structures (linked list vs hash table) depends on the specific requirements of your application. Linked lists are good for insertion and deletion operations, but lookup is O(n). Hash tables offer faster lookup times (O(1)), but require more memory to store pointers. You can experiment with both to see which works best in your situation.

